# A door joining two rooms (Engine v2 T2, #2641). The door's parent is the hall, the side it belongs to (contract
# T1); a typed link joins it to the kitchen. Written: 1 the Souls this world knows, 2 audiences (id: members),
# 3 nodes {1 id, 2 kind (plain; stored as T3's namespace:name@hash), 3 parent, 4 slot, 5 audience, 6 fields},
# 4 links {1 id, 2 type, 3 [end, end], 4 owning end (0 or 1), 5 audience}. Ids are counters: a counter listed in
# section 1 is a Soul (the directory's scope), any other is in the scope of this world's one zone writer. An
# audience is an id or "everyone"; a node written without one has everyone.
{
  1: [],
  2: {},
  3: [
    {1: 1, 2: "souls:place"},
    {1: 2, 2: "souls:room", 3: 1, 6: {1: "hall"}},
    {1: 3, 2: "souls:room", 3: 1, 6: {1: "kitchen"}},
    {1: 4, 2: "souls:door", 3: 2, 6: {1: 1}},             # field 1: open
    {1: 5, 2: "souls:body", 3: 2}
  ],
  4: [
    {1: 6, 2: "leads-to", 3: [4, 3], 4: 0, 5: "everyone"}          # the door to the kitchen, owned by the door's end
  ]
}
